# 7.2.acuity.envelope.sameday.stone

## .what

set the **same-day / near-term tier** — which live scenarios do not force emergency care but should
not wait, and the window in which they should be seen. this is the middle band of the acuity
envelope, above watchful wait and below the emergency floor.

## .inputs

- `7.1.acuity.envelope.emergency.yield.md` — the emergency floor already set
- `6.1.scenario.superposition.bounds.yield.md` — the worst-case bounds
- `6.2.scenario.superposition.prevention.yield.md` — the recurrence likelihoods

## .do

- for the live scenarios below the emergency floor, identify those whose worst-case bound worsens
  over **days** (not hours) — these set the same-day / near-term tier
- state the **time window** (e.g. seen within 24–48h) and name the scenario that drives it
- write the **escalate-sooner signs** — the observations that would lift a same-day case to emergency

## .emit

into `7.2.acuity.envelope.sameday.yield.md` — the same-day tier, its window, the scenario that drives
it, and the escalate-sooner signs.

## .done when

the same-day tier is stated with its window, the scenario that drives it is named, and the
escalate-sooner signs are listed.
